# Product feed for Google Merchant Center and Meta Commerce, generated by the
# backend from the same catalogue — so a price edited in admin reaches the ad
# platforms on their next crawl. Returns 404 until it is enabled in
# Admin → Ops → Product Feed.
/feed.xml  https://frontend-production-a1bd.up.railway.app/api/feed.xml  200
# Favicons come from the backend so the icon set in Admin → Ops → SEO is what
# Google downloads — its favicon fetcher reads these URLs directly and never runs
# the SPA's code. The trailing "!" is required: these files also exist in the
# build, and Netlify serves a matching static file instead of applying a rule
# unless the rule is forced. The backend falls back to the shipped icon.
/favicon.ico  https://frontend-production-a1bd.up.railway.app/api/favicon/favicon.ico  200!
